WEBVTT

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:06.790
Shit, the battle's already begun!

00:00:06.790 --> 00:00:08.110
What happened at the north gate?

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:10.560
The Fabnirs are in pieces!

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:11.820
Hold on tight!

00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:29.430
Use the buildings as cover and keep moving!

00:00:29.430 --> 00:00:30.550
Double-time it to the rendezvous point!

00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:32.030
Colonel Io!

00:00:32.030 --> 00:00:34.050
Leto, continue to cover our flank!

00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:38.690
Now! Charge!

00:00:38.690 --> 00:00:39.240
Colonel!

00:00:42.130 --> 00:00:43.940
I'll stay here and cover you, sir!

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:48.580
We made it here faster than anticipated. All of you can handle the rest.

00:00:48.580 --> 00:00:49.940
Cover me, Leto!

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:51.370
Yes, sir!

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:56.100
Borcuse!

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:01.240
You just don't get it, do you?

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:05.590
You've already failed to protect the palace.

00:01:08.970 --> 00:01:10.280
Borcuse!

00:03:15.470 --> 00:03:17.200
R-Rygart!

00:03:22.110 --> 00:03:24.070
If it isn't the Black Golem.

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:27.190
You know, I've never once seen you fire a pressure gun.

00:03:30.620 --> 00:03:32.300
Borcuse.

00:03:32.300 --> 00:03:35.010
Is it a unique trait of your mysterious golem?

00:03:35.940 --> 00:03:38.720
Or a lack of ability on the part of its pilot?

00:03:39.210 --> 00:03:41.140
Borcuse!

00:03:41.140 --> 00:03:44.870
But I think I'll wait until after I've taken the palace to find out.

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:54.130
I've no intention of fighting unarmed.

00:03:54.130 --> 00:03:55.270
It's just a waste of time.

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:01.220
Be sure not to leave any slack.

00:04:01.220 --> 00:04:03.170
Lady Sigyn, please stand back!

00:04:03.170 --> 00:04:03.550
Tighter!

00:04:04.280 --> 00:04:05.220
Are you sure?

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:08.200
Lady Sigyn, the Delphine has returned.

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:09.420
How's its armor?

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:12.510
Some was obtained and equipped while it was on standby.

00:04:31.510 --> 00:04:34.670
I've read countless times that in the olden days of warfare,

00:04:34.670 --> 00:04:39.350
it often came down to people throwing stones at each other.

00:04:41.250 --> 00:04:43.520
But I never thought I'd be a part of that!

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:53.100
<i>This isn't good. My arm's going to be destroyed!</i>

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:55.410
I recall reading about this as well.

00:04:55.410 --> 00:04:58.250
A sort of hand-to-hand warfare.

00:05:03.860 --> 00:05:05.630
Very good defense!

00:05:05.630 --> 00:05:08.200
Not good enough to defend your whole nation though.

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:12.340
Let's begin the assembly!

00:05:14.150 --> 00:05:18.150
Wind them up as tight as possible to ensure the ligament's strength.

00:05:35.620 --> 00:05:38.910
It seems I was mistaken.

00:05:38.910 --> 00:05:43.700
Indeed, the Black Golem's power, which my nation

00:05:43.700 --> 00:05:46.290
and I find so perplexing, does not owe itself to its pilot.

00:05:46.910 --> 00:05:53.220
But in your own way, you are equally foreign to us.

00:05:53.220 --> 00:05:57.720
A relic of civilizations past reborn, perhaps?

00:05:58.100 --> 00:05:59.400
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:02.200
There's no telling what other
weapons he might be carrying.

00:06:12.590 --> 00:06:14.210
We've lost too much time!

00:06:14.210 --> 00:06:17.010
We'll circle around and attack at the crossroads!

00:06:17.010 --> 00:06:19.430
All right! Time to let loose!

00:06:20.990 --> 00:06:22.090
Beautiful, isn't it?

00:06:22.690 --> 00:06:23.370
Huh?

00:06:23.370 --> 00:06:25.680
The palace is glistening.

00:06:26.590 --> 00:06:29.200
Yeah! We won't let them get near it!

00:06:45.510 --> 00:06:46.630
I just don't understand.

00:06:49.630 --> 00:06:53.940
You don't even understand how to fight!
What's wrong with you?

00:07:08.990 --> 00:07:11.380
Tertiary defense lines have been breached!

00:07:11.380 --> 00:07:13.140
We're fighting off forces coming from the west!

00:07:13.140 --> 00:07:15.990
Enemy squads from the east are
advancing towards the city center!

00:07:19.460 --> 00:07:20.750
I have to get back to them!

00:07:24.910 --> 00:07:29.660
Unbelievable! How can something so heavy even move?

00:07:32.670 --> 00:07:33.890
You little prick!

00:07:38.800 --> 00:07:42.060
But why not take the pressure gun?

00:07:42.060 --> 00:07:45.060
He should be able to manipulate the quartz, right?

00:07:49.100 --> 00:07:54.290
I had heard about people with no powers,

00:07:54.290 --> 00:08:00.000
but I've never met one of the rare individuals before.

00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:04.010
Hey, mister!

00:08:05.290 --> 00:08:06.170
You alive?

00:08:06.170 --> 00:08:07.050
Yeah.

00:08:07.740 --> 00:08:09.030
Want me to call for help?

00:08:09.030 --> 00:08:10.990
That won't be necessary.

00:08:10.990 --> 00:08:14.840
More importantly, kid,
you need to find somewhere to hide.

00:08:14.840 --> 00:08:16.590
The city's swarming with Athens' soldiers.

00:08:16.590 --> 00:08:17.450
Okay.

00:08:24.110 --> 00:08:26.640
Are you Cleo Zaubraff of the Zess Squadron?

00:08:28.030 --> 00:08:30.250
I am Io, of the Borcuse Battalion.

00:08:30.250 --> 00:08:34.860
Yes, I'm Cleo, of Zess—
I mean, the Valkyrie squadron!

00:08:34.860 --> 00:08:35.610
Are you hurt?

00:08:35.610 --> 00:08:37.800
No, I'm fine.

00:08:37.800 --> 00:08:39.620
I promise I'll get you back to Athens.

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:41.610
Just leave the rest to me.

00:08:42.550 --> 00:08:44.090
Thank you very much!

00:09:04.100 --> 00:09:07.350
<i>Goodbye, Sigyn.</i>

00:09:10.960 --> 00:09:12.330
<i>That's the guy from before!</i>

00:09:12.330 --> 00:09:14.020
I'll finish you off this time!

00:09:18.220 --> 00:09:20.340
There's no end to these bastards!

00:09:26.180 --> 00:09:27.510
Let's get moving.

00:09:27.510 --> 00:09:28.530
You mean this giant thing?

00:09:29.350 --> 00:09:33.510
I know, it's rather primitive for a weapon.

00:09:33.510 --> 00:09:36.030
That's kind of an understatement.

00:09:36.030 --> 00:09:40.620
But the truth is the pilot, Rygart Arrow, can't use magic.

00:09:40.620 --> 00:09:41.630
What?

00:09:42.750 --> 00:09:44.440
Then how does he fight?

00:09:44.440 --> 00:09:49.540
The Delphine was a product of the bygone
civilization and extremely difficult to maneuver.

00:09:49.540 --> 00:09:54.530
But for some reason, only the powerless Rygart, scorned for his lack of magic, can make it move.

00:09:55.000 --> 00:09:57.850
And we've yet to understand why.

00:09:58.440 --> 00:10:05.600
But despite that, he can still use this weapon somehow.

00:10:05.600 --> 00:10:10.000
I think, it's just because he's strange.

00:10:11.410 --> 00:10:13.490
All preparations complete!

00:10:24.850 --> 00:10:26.880
One born without the gift of magic...

00:10:29.060 --> 00:10:30.400
Lady Sigyn!

00:10:31.130 --> 00:10:32.580
<i>He's</i> the strange one?

00:10:32.580 --> 00:10:33.870
Everyone to the first inner gate!

00:10:33.870 --> 00:10:34.820
We need to get it to the gate asap!

00:10:36.510 --> 00:10:37.320
Rygart!

00:10:43.930 --> 00:10:45.060
Sigyn?

00:10:46.450 --> 00:10:47.990
Take it!

00:10:47.990 --> 00:10:50.780
Over there, Rygart! Take it!

00:11:01.760 --> 00:11:03.250
Let's see what you can do.

00:11:10.610 --> 00:11:13.140
It's extremely dangerous here. Please fall back.

00:11:13.140 --> 00:11:16.170
Are you mad?! You first, Lady Sigyn!

00:11:16.170 --> 00:11:19.980
We cannot return until you do!

00:11:35.430 --> 00:11:37.040
What a splendidly fitting weapon for you!

00:11:48.680 --> 00:11:51.180
Damn, why won't he go down already?!

00:11:58.310 --> 00:11:58.750
Colonel!

00:12:03.360 --> 00:12:05.470
I'm sorry, but this is as far as I can go.

00:12:05.470 --> 00:12:06.860
Please escape on your own!

00:12:07.280 --> 00:12:11.130
I'll take care of this one,
so you've got to survive at all costs!

00:12:11.130 --> 00:12:11.780
But Colonel!

00:12:11.780 --> 00:12:12.890
Get going!

00:12:20.910 --> 00:12:21.590
Bastard!

00:12:27.130 --> 00:12:28.410
Don't get so cocky!

00:12:41.600 --> 00:12:42.650
Loggin!

00:12:43.690 --> 00:12:44.610
S'cuse me!

00:12:45.540 --> 00:12:47.120
Let me handle this, okay?

00:13:01.530 --> 00:13:02.440
Damn, that's heavy!

00:13:02.440 --> 00:13:03.670
Nile!

00:13:03.670 --> 00:13:06.470
Don't just stand there!
They're attacking the secondary castle walls!

00:13:06.470 --> 00:13:07.150
Right!

00:13:07.150 --> 00:13:09.090
Nile!

00:13:09.660 --> 00:13:11.610
I just had a score to settle with him, that's all.

00:13:12.040 --> 00:13:13.570
And trust me, we're even now.

00:13:13.570 --> 00:13:14.660
You're insane.

00:13:14.660 --> 00:13:15.560
Loggin, behind you!

00:13:19.200 --> 00:13:20.250
Let's go!

00:13:22.000 --> 00:13:24.060
<i>We'll finish this next time.</i>

00:13:35.350 --> 00:13:36.210
Lady Sigyn!

00:13:36.210 --> 00:13:37.610
Please, let me down here!

00:13:37.610 --> 00:13:38.570
We can't!

00:13:38.570 --> 00:13:40.710
The Delphine needs our help!

00:13:40.710 --> 00:13:42.640
Closing the primary castle walls!

00:14:18.100 --> 00:14:19.350
Tenacious little bugger.

00:14:27.750 --> 00:14:29.860
Just what are you made of, pal?

00:14:58.960 --> 00:15:00.320
Rygart...

00:15:00.320 --> 00:15:04.970
Even the mighty Borcuse is
caught off guard by your weapon.

00:15:05.900 --> 00:15:08.030
What are you doing, King Hodr?!

00:15:08.030 --> 00:15:08.930
Come back inside at once!

00:15:09.890 --> 00:15:12.470
What're you doing? You could be shot!

00:15:12.470 --> 00:15:13.260
Minister.

00:15:13.260 --> 00:15:13.640
Milord?

00:15:14.300 --> 00:15:18.510
That brainless idiot Rygart is fighting to the death.

00:15:19.560 --> 00:15:20.750
For the sake of our nation.

00:15:23.280 --> 00:15:27.770
He's fighting an enemy general
in a golem we know nothing about.

00:15:27.770 --> 00:15:29.570
And I ordered him to do it.

00:15:30.160 --> 00:15:34.800
No, that's not true. I asked him to.

00:15:35.660 --> 00:15:40.220
I gave him the option to refuse,
yet he still took up arms.

00:15:40.710 --> 00:15:43.300
With his own hands, devoid of magic.

00:15:46.600 --> 00:15:50.500
Compared to that, standing in the rain is nothing.

00:16:05.780 --> 00:16:08.530
I can see the limitations of your weapon.

00:16:12.040 --> 00:16:14.510
How can the ligaments be wound so tightly?

00:16:38.500 --> 00:16:39.880
Rygart!

00:16:40.230 --> 00:16:41.730
Lady Sigyn!

00:16:41.730 --> 00:16:42.580
Unhand me!

00:16:42.580 --> 00:16:43.520
You can't go out there!

00:16:49.020 --> 00:16:53.030
Show yourself! Who <i>are</i> you?!

00:16:53.030 --> 00:16:55.040
Let me see the kind of freak you are!

00:17:30.250 --> 00:17:31.450
Too slow!

00:17:47.650 --> 00:17:48.980
The Black Golem...

00:18:16.970 --> 00:18:21.420
<i>Don't worry Leda, Io will still come to your recital. </i>

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:06.900
Just before mid-day, word of
General Borcuse's death reached his battalion,

00:19:06.900 --> 00:19:10.200
and they made a temporary retreat.

00:19:10.200 --> 00:19:16.200
It didn't take long for the news
to reach Secretary General Loquis.

00:19:19.470 --> 00:19:20.220
Cleo's alive?

00:19:20.220 --> 00:19:22.400
Yes, sir. She's unharmed.

00:19:22.400 --> 00:19:26.800
She was seen escaping Binonten onboard a trade vessel.

00:19:26.800 --> 00:19:28.200
Where is she now?

00:19:28.200 --> 00:19:30.060
Her whereabouts are currently unknown.

00:19:30.060 --> 00:19:31.160
I can't just leave her to fend for herself.

00:19:32.270 --> 00:19:35.030
Let's form a search party immediately.

00:19:35.030 --> 00:19:36.540
But what about your leg?

00:19:36.540 --> 00:19:39.390
I'll be fine. I'll go convince my brother.

00:19:39.390 --> 00:19:41.050
Are you coming with me?

00:19:41.050 --> 00:19:42.100
Of course!

00:19:42.630 --> 00:19:43.980
Dear?

00:19:45.200 --> 00:19:46.490
I won't be gone long.

00:19:53.300 --> 00:19:55.460
Stop it, Narvi!

00:19:57.040 --> 00:20:00.600
Why?! Why did General True have to die?!

00:20:01.030 --> 00:20:04.610
Don't beat yourself up over it!
There's nothing we could've done!

00:20:06.580 --> 00:20:08.970
He's long gone, okay?!

00:20:09.830 --> 00:20:10.890
Narvi.

00:20:16.430 --> 00:20:17.680
Loggin.

00:20:19.680 --> 00:20:20.750
Tragic, I know.

00:20:29.450 --> 00:20:30.680
Can you stand?

00:20:30.680 --> 00:20:33.820
Yeah, I'm fine. Just a few scrapes.

00:20:36.920 --> 00:20:38.100
Rygart.

00:20:38.100 --> 00:20:39.720
I came back.

00:20:40.920 --> 00:20:42.220
Just like I promised.

00:20:48.650 --> 00:20:51.250
It's not over yet, though. Right?

00:20:52.240 --> 00:20:53.240
Rygart.

00:20:54.670 --> 00:20:58.230
Zess will be back, won't he?

00:21:05.680 --> 00:21:11.230
We'll have to fight each other again.

00:21:13.620 --> 00:21:14.760
Bro!

00:21:15.710 --> 00:21:17.760
That was <i>you</i> riding that thing?!

00:21:18.300 --> 00:21:21.380
Regarz! You're alive?!

00:21:21.650 --> 00:21:23.580
That's all you have to say?!

00:21:23.580 --> 00:21:27.390
You never came back,
so I went looking all over for you!

00:21:29.400 --> 00:21:32.000
You said “I'm going to the capital” and that was it!

00:21:33.740 --> 00:21:39.840
What the hell have you been doing this whole time?!
